  <section>
    <h2>Overview: An Honest Update</h2>
    <p>Dover-Foxcroft is the county seat of Piscataquis County, Maine. The town sits along the Piscataquis River at the outlet of Sebec Lake, in the central Maine interior. Population ~4,200. Dover-Foxcroft is on US Route 6 / Route 7, midway between Bangor (45 min south) and Greenville / Moosehead Lake (60 min north).</p>
    <p>The MDG Dover-Foxcroft guide previously claimed the town has had a cannabis dispensary — Dab Bar and Dispensary Dover-Foxcroft — operating since 2020. That claim was sourced from a directory listing (DabBars.org) that is no longer reliable: the dabbars.org domain is now a parked GoDaddy placeholder, and the operator's own web presence has lapsed. The medicalmarijuanadispensaries.co directory returns 0 dispensary results for Dover-Foxcroft, ME 04426 as of mid-2026. Yelp's 2026 Dover-Foxcroft search returns operators physically located in Bass Harbor, Howland, and other nearby towns, not Dover-Foxcroft proper.</p>
    <p>This revised guide reflects that uncertainty rather than continue to claim a specific Dover-Foxcroft storefront that cannot be verified. The town's opt-in status remains confirmed on the Maine Cannabis Opt-In Tracker, and the broader Piscataquis County cannabis market is well-served by GreenLife in Milo, Puffers Place in Dexter, and Hazy Moose in Howland. For current local dispensary status in Dover-Foxcroft proper, contact the Piscataquis County Chamber of Commerce or the City of Dover-Foxcroft directly.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>The Piscataquis County Cannabis Corridor</h2>
    <p>Dover-Foxcroft sits at the center of Piscataquis County's broader cannabis market. The county's three dispensary operators are:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>GreenLife Recreational Dispensary</strong> — 19 Park Street, Milo, ME 04463 (phone 207-943-9005). Owned by Bob Ade, Piscataquis Chamber's 2022 Business of the Year for his Pat's Pizza franchises in Dover-Foxcroft and Milo. Opened April 13, 2023. Adult-use. Per the Piscataquis Chamber listing.</li>
      <li><strong>Puffers Place</strong> — 50 Johnson Road, Dexter, ME 04930 (phone 207-270-1064). Medical dispensary with on-site 420-friendly lakefront rental on Puffers Pond. Serves a 33-town catchment per the operator's site that includes Dover-Foxcroft, Milo, Brownville, and surrounding Piscataquis towns.</li>
      <li><strong>Hazy Moose Medical Cannabis Dispensary</strong> — 22 Main St, Howland, ME (per Yelp). Established 2022. Serves medical cannabis patients with craft cannabis products. Multi-location (Howland, Monticello, Bangor).</li>
    </ul>
    <p>For Piscataquis County residents, the GreenLife / Puffers Place / Hazy Moose cluster provides adult-use and medical access without requiring travel to Bangor. For Bangor-area dispensaries, Bangor is ~45 min south with multiple storefronts including Curaleaf, Firestorm, and others.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Service Area</h2>
    <p>Dover-Foxcroft dispensaries (current and historical) have served a large central Maine interior geographic area. Common drive-times from downtown Dover-Foxcroft:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Milo</strong> — 15 min south (GreenLife adult-use)</li>
      <li><strong>Sebec</strong> — 10 min south</li>
